<title>BELGIUM: Denmark to press for early agreement on generic food.</title>
<headline>Denmark to press for early agreement on generic food.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark is to press on Monday for an early agreement on the European Commission's pledge to establish a new five-year transition period for geographically designated foods, an EU official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The original proposal from the Council in 1992 set a five- year transition period but the Commission proposal did not appear until May last year.</p>
<p>&quot;As a result the Commisson said it would make a proposal at the September farm Council for the five years to begin from the date of their own proposal's publication,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The issue is not listed for Monday's farm Council and Denmark will raise it and say they want it agreed quickly, the official added.</p>
</text>
